   "h": "Who the Center serves",
   "text": "Families the Center's social team classes as vulnerable: income below the minimum wage, homes without running water or electricity, single-parent (especially single-mother) households, more than two dependents per earner, and adolescent pregnancy. ✅ (c4wf.org, *Center info*). The current page lists **223 families**, an average of 5 members each and an average family income of just over $360 a month. ⚠️ The page is undated. Earlier figures: about 400 families (Opus Prize, 2010), 323 families and 885 children (2020 council file), and more than 300 (2021, 2023).",
