 "web": "These barriers land on one household at once. Take a pattern, not a person. A mother in north Quito sews piecework at home because the formal job she trained for starts at 7 a.m. and the child-development center takes only children aged 1–3. No contract means no IESS, and no IESS means no paid sick days and no pension. The house has two finished rooms and a third wall waiting for the next minga. In October 2024 her machine sat idle up to 14 hours a day. The corner shop where she buys thread pays someone every week. Her brother left for the US in 2023. No one barrier decided her life. Together they set the price.",
