   "contested": "This is the most honestly contested barrier on the trip. Halligan said in 2009 that child laborers have always existed and always will (NCR). His model fed, schooled and protected working children instead of forbidding their work. After 2015 the Center began replacing work-based programming because of the government's enforcement. ✅ (c4wf.org). Whether the earlier model or the later law served children better is a real question. Students should hold it, not settle it. Put both truths on the page at once: some families in the Center's community need a child's income in some weeks, and a child who works is more likely to leave school. A rule that bans the work without replacing the income moves the problem; it doesn't solve it.",
